// Every `asm` function must have a body for the triple this build selected.
//
// That question used to be asked inside each target's emission loop, which
// made it unanswerable cleanly: `print` and the generated code share one
// stream, so the diagnostic landed in the middle of the C and the build died
// as "internal error: the self-hosted compiler emitted C that does not
// compile" -- a portability problem reported as a compiler bug. It belongs
// here instead, beside the other gate, where a failure means nothing is
// written at all.
// Both targets select asm bodies the same way, so the check is neither one's;
// asm_check itself reports only on a name's first row.
check_asm_targets(int argc, string[] argv) {
  string arg_triple_v = arg_triple(argc, argv);
  int i = 0;
  while(i < asm_count()) {
    asm_check(i, arg_triple_v);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return void;
